## Component Documentation

### SmartContractSystem
The main container component for smart contract documentation.

Props:
- `network`: string - The blockchain network (e.g., "Ethereum")
- `architecture`: string - The system architecture type
- `description`: string - A brief description of the system

### ContractSection
Represents a major section of smart contract components.

Props:
- `title`: string - The section title
- `type`: 'core' | 'auxiliary' | 'governance' - The type of contract section
- `description`: string - A brief description of the section's purpose

### ContractComponent
Represents a specific smart contract component.

Props:
- `name`: string - The component name
- `type`: 'token' | 'pricing' | 'supply' | 'governance' | 'factory' | 'treasury' | 'access' - The type of component
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the component's purpose
- `implementation`: 'On-chain' | 'Off-chain' - Where the component is implemented

### OffChainComponents
Container for off-chain system components.

### OffChainComponent
Represents a specific off-chain component.

Props:
- `name`: string - The component name
- `type`: 'oracle' | 'tracking' | 'computation' - The type of component
- `importance`: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' - The importance level
- `description`: string - A brief description of the component's purpose
- `implementation`: 'On-chain' | 'Off-chain' - Where the component is implemented

## Usage Example

```tsx
<SmartContractSystem
  network="Ethereum"
  architecture="Hybrid"
  description="Example smart contract system"
>
  <ContractSection
    title="Example Section"
    type="core"
    description="Example contract section"
  >
    <ContractComponent
      name="Example Component"
      type="token"
      importance="high"
      description="Example component description"
      implementation="On-chain"
    />
  </ContractSection>
</SmartContractSystem>
```

## Notes
- All on-chain components should be thoroughly audited
- Off-chain components should have clear integration points
- Maintain clear separation between on-chain and off-chain logic
- Document all security considerations
- Include gas optimization guidelines
- Specify upgrade mechanisms where applicable
- Document emergency procedures
